From: LYW-30M local development <local@localhost>
Subject: ath11k: guard CE RX ring access after firmware recovery

The CE TX completion path already rejects a cleared source ring when
recovery races a completion callback. Apply the same check to the CE
destination path before ath11k_hal_srng_dst_get_next_entry(). During
firmware crash teardown hal_srng_clear() can remove the destination tail
pointer while a late callback is still being serviced. Treat that as an
empty/error receive and let the existing replenish path rebuild buffers.
No ring sizes, skb allocation policy, firmware ABI or normal data path is
changed.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ce.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ce.c
@@ -418,6 +418,16 @@ static int ath11k_ce_completed_recv_next(struct ath11k_ce_pipe *pipe,
	srng = &ab->hal.srng_list[pipe->status_ring->hal_ring_id];
 
	spin_lock_bh(&srng->lock);
 
+	/*
+	 * Recovery can clear a destination ring while a late CE callback is
+	 * being serviced. The TX completion path has the same guard for its
+	 * source ring. Do not dereference the cleared tail pointer.
+	 */
+	if (unlikely(!srng->u.dst_ring.tp_addr)) {
+		ret = -EIO;
+		goto err;
+	}
+
 	ath11k_hal_srng_access_begin(ab, srng);
